    "extracted text": "The sheets were subjected to solution treatment at 470°C for 2 h, water quenched, and then aged at 120°C and 150°C from 1 h to 72 h. The 7055 and 7055-0.25Sc alloys exhibited a hardening behavior, and the peak-aged times of these two alloys were in the range of 24-26 h during aging at 120°C. The peak-aged times of the 7055 and 7055-0.25Sc alloys were reduced to 8 and 5 h, respectively, when the aging temperature was increased to 150°C. Tensile properties were measured for both alloys after aging at 120°C for 24h, 150°C for 8h, and 150°C for 30h.",
